IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb2-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part X, sections 121 to 123 -- OFFICERS, THE DUTY OF
-- CARE OF DIRECTORS AND OFFICERS, AND DISSENT. Layer 1.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RULE. Named `<what it works out> within s <section>`. Where a provision says what follows in
-- a stated case, the rule is TRUE when that case holds; FALSE means only that this provision does not apply.
-- A rule whose result is a MAYBE returns NOTHING where the text is silent for the case.
-- Within this module a rule that depends on a sibling calls it and takes its inputs. A cross-reference to
-- another piece is a plain input and says so.

§ `s 121 Officers`

§§ `s 121 Officers`

DECLARE `Power of the directors over officers under s 121(a)` IS ONE OF
    `designating the offices of the corporation`
    `appointing as officers persons of full capacity`
    `specifying the duties of officers`
    `delegating to officers powers to manage the business and affairs of the corporation`

-- "Subject to the articles, the by-laws or any unanimous shareholder agreement." Delegation is "except powers to
-- do anything referred to in subsection 115(3)" (fork F-P10-14).
-- src:1480 | Officers
-- src:1481 | 121 Subject to the articles, the by-laws or any unanimous shareholder agreement,
-- src:1482 | (a) the directors may designate the offices of the corporation, appoint as officers persons of full capacity, specify their duties and delegate to them powers to manage the business and affairs of the corporation, except powers to do anything referred to in subsection 115(3);
@ref CBCA s 121 (src:1480-1482)
GIVEN `the power` IS A `Power of the directors over officers under s 121(a)`
      `the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person to be appointed is of full capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power to be delegated is one to do something referred to in subsection 115(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors have the power over officers within s 121(a)` MEANS
        (NOT `the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provide`)
    AND (CONSIDER `the power`
         WHEN `designating the offices of the corporation` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `appointing as officers persons of full capacity` THEN `the person to be appointed is of full capacity`
         WHEN `specifying the duties of officers` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `delegating to officers powers to manage the business and affairs of the corporation` THEN NOT `the power to be delegated is one to do something referred to in subsection 115(3)`)

-- src:1481 | 121 Subject to the articles, the by-laws or any unanimous shareholder agreement,
-- src:1483 | (b) a director may be appointed to any office of the corporation; and
@ref CBCA s 121 (src:1481 src:1483)
GIVEN `the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a director may be appointed to an office of the corporation within s 121(b)` MEANS
    NOT `the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provide`

-- src:1481 | 121 Subject to the articles, the by-laws or any unanimous shareholder agreement,
-- src:1484 | (c) two or more offices of the corporation may be held by the same person.
@ref CBCA s 121 (src:1481 src:1484)
GIVEN `the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`two or more offices of the corporation may be held by the same person within s 121(c)` MEANS
    NOT `the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provide`

§ `s 122 Duty of care of directors and officers`

§§ `s 122(1) Duty of care of directors and officers`

-- src:1485 | Duty of care of directors and officers
-- src:1486 | 122 (1) Every director and officer of a corporation in exercising their powers and discharging their duties shall
-- src:1487 | (a) act honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation; and
-- src:1488 | (b) exercise the care, diligence and skill that a reasonably prudent person would exercise in comparable circumstances.
@ref CBCA s 122(1) (src:1485-1488)
GIVEN `the person acts honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person exercises the care, diligence and skill that a reasonably prudent person would exercise in comparable circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the director or officer has discharged the duty of care within s 122(1)` MEANS
        `the person acts honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation`
    AND `the person exercises the care, diligence and skill that a reasonably prudent person would exercise in comparable circumstances`

§§ `s 122(1.1) Best interests of the corporation`

DECLARE `Factor the directors and officers may consider under s 122(1.1)` IS ONE OF
    `the interests of shareholders`
    `the interests of employees`
    `the interests of retirees and pensioners`
    `the interests of creditors`
    `the interests of consumers`
    `the interests of governments`
    `the environment`
    `the long-term interests of the corporation`

-- "May consider, but are not limited to": this list is not exhaustive. Any other relevant factor may be
-- considered too, which the list does not show.
-- src:1489 | Best interests of the corporation
-- src:1490 | (1.1) When acting with a view to the best interests of the corporation under paragraph (1)(a), the directors and officers of the corporation may consider, but are not limited to, the following factors:
-- src:1491 | (a) the interests of
-- src:1492 | (i) shareholders,
-- src:1493 | (ii) employees,
-- src:1494 | (iii) retirees and pensioners,
-- src:1495 | (iv) creditors,
-- src:1496 | (v) consumers, and
-- src:1497 | (vi) governments;
-- src:1498 | (b) the environment; and
-- src:1499 | (c) the long-term interests of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 122(1.1) (src:1489-1499)
GIVEN `the person is acting with a view to the best interests of the corporation under paragraph 122(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Factor the directors and officers may consider under s 122(1.1)`
`the factors listed that the directors and officers may consider within s 122(1.1)` MEANS
    IF `the person is acting with a view to the best interests of the corporation under paragraph 122(1)(a)`
    THEN LIST `the interests of shareholders`, `the interests of employees`, `the interests of retirees and pensioners`,
              `the interests of creditors`, `the interests of consumers`, `the interests of governments`,
              `the environment`, `the long-term interests of the corporation`
    ELSE EMPTY

§§ `s 122(2) Duty to comply`

-- src:1500 | Duty to comply
-- src:1501 | (2) Every director and officer of a corporation shall comply with this Act, the regulations, articles, by-laws and any unanimous shareholder agreement.
@ref CBCA s 122(2) (src:1500-1501)
GIVEN `the person complies with the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person complies with the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person complies with the articles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person complies with the by-laws` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person complies with any unanimous shareholder agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the director or officer has complied with the duty to comply within s 122(2)` MEANS
        `the person complies with the Act`
    AND `the person complies with the regulations`
    AND `the person complies with the articles`
    AND `the person complies with the by-laws`
    AND `the person complies with any unanimous shareholder agreement`

§§ `s 122(3) No exculpation`

-- Subject to subsection 146(5) (out of range: section 146 (piece cb3)): a provision there is allowed to do what
-- this subsection otherwise forbids. TRUE: the provision does not relieve the director or officer.
-- src:1502 | No exculpation
-- src:1503 | (3) Subject to subsection 146(5), no provision in a contract, the articles, the by-laws or a resolution relieves a director or officer from the duty to act in accordance with this Act or the regulations or relieves them from liability for a breach thereof.
@ref CBCA s 122(3) (src:1502-1503)
GIVEN `the provision is in a contract, the articles, the by-laws or a resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision purports to relieve the director or officer from the duty to act in accordance with the Act or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision purports to relieve the director or officer from liability for a breach of that duty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is permitted by subsection 146(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the provision does not relieve the director or officer within s 122(3)` MEANS
        `the provision is in a contract, the articles, the by-laws or a resolution`
    AND (   `the provision purports to relieve the director or officer from the duty to act in accordance with the Act or the regulations`
         OR `the provision purports to relieve the director or officer from liability for a breach of that duty`)
    AND (NOT `the provision is permitted by subsection 146(5)`)

§ `s 123 Dissent`

§§ `s 123(1) Dissent`

-- src:1504 | Dissent
-- src:1505 | 123 (1) A director who is present at a meeting of directors or committee of directors is deemed to have consented to any resolution passed or action taken at the meeting unless
-- src:1506 | (a) the director requests a dissent to be entered in the minutes of the meeting, or the dissent has been entered in the minutes;
-- src:1507 | (b) the director sends a written dissent to the secretary of the meeting before the meeting is adjourned; or
-- src:1508 | (c) the director sends a dissent by registered mail or delivers it to the registered office of the corporation immediately after the meeting is adjourned.
@ref CBCA s 123(1) (src:1504-1508)
GIVEN `the director is present at the meeting of directors or committee of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director requests a dissent to be entered in the minutes of the meeting, or the dissent has been entered in the minutes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director sends a written dissent to the secretary of the meeting before the meeting is adjourned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director sends a dissent by registered mail or delivers it to the registered office of the corporation immediately after the meeting is adjourned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the director is deemed to have consented to the resolution or action within s 123(1)` MEANS
        `the director is present at the meeting of directors or committee of directors`
    AND (NOT (   `the director requests a dissent to be entered in the minutes of the meeting, or the dissent has been entered in the minutes`
              OR `the director sends a written dissent to the secretary of the meeting before the meeting is adjourned`
              OR `the director sends a dissent by registered mail or delivers it to the registered office of the corporation immediately after the meeting is adjourned`))

§§ `s 123(2) Loss of right to dissent`

-- src:1509 | Loss of right to dissent
-- src:1510 | (2) A director who votes for or consents to a resolution is not entitled to dissent under subsection (1).
@ref CBCA s 123(2) (src:1509-1510)
GIVEN `the director votes for or consents to the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the director is entitled to dissent under subsection 123(1) within s 123(2)` MEANS
    NOT `the director votes for or consents to the resolution`

-- The two together, for a director who was present: consented (in fact, or deemed) unless entitled to dissent
-- and one of the ways of dissenting in (1) was used.
-- src:1504 | Dissent
-- src:1505 | 123 (1) A director who is present at a meeting of directors or committee of directors is deemed to have consented to any resolution passed or action taken at the meeting unless
-- src:1506 | (a) the director requests a dissent to be entered in the minutes of the meeting, or the dissent has been entered in the minutes;
-- src:1507 | (b) the director sends a written dissent to the secretary of the meeting before the meeting is adjourned; or
-- src:1508 | (c) the director sends a dissent by registered mail or delivers it to the registered office of the corporation immediately after the meeting is adjourned.
-- src:1509 | Loss of right to dissent
-- src:1510 | (2) A director who votes for or consents to a resolution is not entitled to dissent under subsection (1).
@ref CBCA s 123(1) s 123(2) (src:1504-1510)
GIVEN `the director is present at the meeting of directors or committee of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director votes for or consents to the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director requests a dissent to be entered in the minutes of the meeting, or the dissent has been entered in the minutes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director sends a written dissent to the secretary of the meeting before the meeting is adjourned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director sends a dissent by registered mail or delivers it to the registered office of the corporation immediately after the meeting is adjourned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the present director is treated as having consented within s 123(1) and (2)` MEANS
        `the director is present at the meeting of directors or committee of directors`
    AND (   `the director votes for or consents to the resolution`
         OR `the director is deemed to have consented to the resolution or action within s 123(1)`
                `the director is present at the meeting of directors or committee of directors`
                `the director requests a dissent to be entered in the minutes of the meeting, or the dissent has been entered in the minutes`
                `the director sends a written dissent to the secretary of the meeting before the meeting is adjourned`
                `the director sends a dissent by registered mail or delivers it to the registered office of the corporation immediately after the meeting is adjourned`)

§§ `s 123(3) Dissent of absent director`

-- The printed text of this subsection repeats a fragment ("the director aware or the resolution, the director");
-- read as "unless within seven days after becoming aware of the resolution, the director (a) ... or (b) ..."
-- (finding in NOTES). Seven days counted by the keel's convention (fork F1).
-- src:1511 | Dissent of absent director
-- src:1512 | (3) A director who was not present at a meeting at which a resolution was passed or action taken is deemed to have consented thereto unless within seven days after becoming aware of the resolution, the director aware or the resolution, the director
-- src:1513 | (a) causes a dissent to be placed with the minutes of the meeting; or
-- src:1514 | (b) sends a dissent by registered mail or delivers it to the registered office of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 123(3) (src:1511-1514)
GIVEN `the director was present at the meeting at which the resolution was passed or action taken` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the director became aware of the resolution` IS A DATE
      `the date the director dissented, if the director did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the director caused a dissent to be placed with the minutes of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director sent a dissent by registered mail or delivered it to the registered office of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the absent director is deemed to have consented within s 123(3)` MEANS
        (NOT `the director was present at the meeting at which the resolution was passed or action taken`)
    AND (NOT (    (   `the director caused a dissent to be placed with the minutes of the meeting`
                   OR `the director sent a dissent by registered mail or delivered it to the registered office of the corporation`)
              AND CONSIDER `the date the director dissented, if the director did`
                  WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
                  WHEN JUST d THEN `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 7, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`)
                                       `the date the director became aware of the resolution` d))

§§ `s 123(4) Defence -- reasonable diligence`

-- "Including reliance in good faith on (a) or (b)": the reliance is an illustration of what the standard
-- includes. It is not a further condition, so the rule takes the standard as one fact (fork F-P10-16).
-- src:1515 | Defence — reasonable diligence
-- src:1516 | (4) A director is not liable under section 118 or 119, and has complied with his or her duties under subsection 122(2), if the director exercised the care, diligence and skill that a reasonably prudent person would have exercised in comparable circumstances, including reliance in good faith on
-- src:1517 | (a) financial statements of the corporation represented to the director by an officer of the corporation or in a written report of the auditor of the corporation fairly to reflect the financial condition of the corporation; or
-- src:1518 | (b) a report of a person whose profession lends credibility to a statement made by the professional person.
@ref CBCA s 123(4) (src:1515-1518)
GIVEN `the director exercised the care, diligence and skill that a reasonably prudent person would have exercised in comparable circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the director is not liable under section 118 or 119 and has complied with subsection 122(2) within s 123(4)` MEANS
    `the director exercised the care, diligence and skill that a reasonably prudent person would have exercised in comparable circumstances`

§§ `s 123(5) Defence -- good faith`

-- src:1519 | Defence — good faith
-- src:1520 | (5) A director has complied with his or her duties under subsection 122(1) if the director relied in good faith on
-- src:1521 | (a) financial statements of the corporation represented to the director by an officer of the corporation or in a written report of the auditor of the corporation fairly to reflect the financial condition of the corporation; or
-- src:1522 | (b) a report of a person whose profession lends credibility to a statement made by the professional person.
@ref CBCA s 123(5) (src:1519-1522)
GIVEN `the director relied in good faith on financial statements of the corporation represented to the director by an officer of the corporation or in a written report of the auditor of the corporation fairly to reflect the financial condition of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director relied in good faith on a report of a person whose profession lends credibility to a statement made by the professional person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the director has complied with subsection 122(1) by reliance in good faith within s 123(5)` MEANS
        `the director relied in good faith on financial statements of the corporation represented to the director by an officer of the corporation or in a written report of the auditor of the corporation fairly to reflect the financial condition of the corporation`
    OR  `the director relied in good faith on a report of a person whose profession lends credibility to a statement made by the professional person`

-- The two ways of complying with subsection 122(1), for a director.
-- src:1485 | Duty of care of directors and officers
-- src:1486 | 122 (1) Every director and officer of a corporation in exercising their powers and discharging their duties shall
-- src:1487 | (a) act honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation; and
-- src:1488 | (b) exercise the care, diligence and skill that a reasonably prudent person would exercise in comparable circumstances.
-- src:1519 | Defence — good faith
-- src:1520 | (5) A director has complied with his or her duties under subsection 122(1) if the director relied in good faith on
-- src:1521 | (a) financial statements of the corporation represented to the director by an officer of the corporation or in a written report of the auditor of the corporation fairly to reflect the financial condition of the corporation; or
-- src:1522 | (b) a report of a person whose profession lends credibility to a statement made by the professional person.
@ref CBCA s 122(1) s 123(5) (src:1485-1488 src:1519-1522)
GIVEN `the person acts honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person exercises the care, diligence and skill that a reasonably prudent person would exercise in comparable circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director relied in good faith on financial statements of the corporation represented to the director by an officer of the corporation or in a written report of the auditor of the corporation fairly to reflect the financial condition of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director relied in good faith on a report of a person whose profession lends credibility to a statement made by the professional person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the director has complied with the duty of care within s 122(1) and 123(5)` MEANS
        `the director or officer has discharged the duty of care within s 122(1)`
            `the person acts honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the corporation`
            `the person exercises the care, diligence and skill that a reasonably prudent person would exercise in comparable circumstances`
    OR  `the director has complied with subsection 122(1) by reliance in good faith within s 123(5)`
            `the director relied in good faith on financial statements of the corporation represented to the director by an officer of the corporation or in a written report of the auditor of the corporation fairly to reflect the financial condition of the corporation`
            `the director relied in good faith on a report of a person whose profession lends credibility to a statement made by the professional person`
